+## S3-TALK (2026-11-15): the Talk screen's speed work, PS1 side
+
+The package is GBA work (docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-TALK"); Talk is not linked on the PS1. Shared code it touched and the
+PS1 links: the S3 output lint (`talk_safe.c`, a pair table and a window: 192 B more stack while a line is linted), `talk_db.c`
+(`plat_talk_image`, weak NULL here), `scene.c` (`scene_keep_below`, off here), `ui.c` (`ui_shadow_kept` is a macro that does
+nothing here) and `ui_dialog.c` (`ui_dialog_reach`). With the boot FMV the EXE ends at `_end` 0x801e04a0: **129,872 B below
+the stack top** against 130,000 B on the tip it was built on (`fe41002`): **+128 B resident**, inside SPEED's 2 KB share, the
+72 KB plan gate met with 56,144 B to spare. `game_smoke` passes (PCSX-Redux).
